  "attribution_note": "Source packing by Alejandro Zarzuelo. Original source credit: soft-to-rigid method by Yohei Nakajima (2026); generalization to Archimedean, Catalan, prism and antiprism solids, basin-hopping search and certification developed with Claude (Anthropic) under Alejandro Zarzuelo's direction.  PingYou Ltd supplies this full-owner axial subdivision and declared whole-child deletion; original source authors and frames are retained.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "complete_parent_axial_subdivision_and_whole_child_prefix",
   "proof": "Exact whole-prism axial subdivision and retained-prefix return\n\nLet a complete parent prism be B times[-H/2,H/2], in center c and\nproper frame R, where H=k*h and k is2 or3. For j=0,...,k-1 define\ndelta_j=(j-(k-1)/2)*h. Then the k whole target prisms with the same\nbase B, height h, frame R and centers c+delta_j*R*e_z have disjoint\ninteriors and their union is the parent. This is an exact physical\nsubdivision. All full target owners are present; there is no fractional\nowner and no new outer end cost. Their pairwise and wall compatibility\nis inherited simultaneously from the complete parent packing.\n\nFor robust native coordinates, use lambda=10000001/10000000. Scale\nthe ideal child centers by lambda while retaining target unit shape\nand frame. Each target child lies strictly inside the homothetic\nlambda-parent: transverse sections are B inside lambda*B, and its\naxial extreme is lambda*|delta_j|+h/2 <=lambda*H/2-(lambda-1)*h/2.\nThe homothetic complete parent packing remains disjoint in a host\nscaled by lambda. The implementation recomputes every actual rounded\nchild center as an exact binary rational, transforms it back through\nthe exact native quaternion, and checks all its canonical vertices\nagainst every lambda-parent face in the common exact number field.\nIt also checks adjacent children using the same actual axial separator.\nThus rounding is covered by actual containment, not an assumed epsilon.\n\nParents are ordered as in the SHA-bound native witness. For each parent\norder children by j. The complete child map and full native child array\nare retained. Keep a declared prefix for a smaller target count; this\ndeletes whole children without moving any other child. Source authors,\nsource frames and the full parent proof remain embedded. The final\nindependent native checker verifies all target owners and target host\nwalls directly. No angle or center optimization occurs in this transfer.\n",
